    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0562" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/1034: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-30T20:00:00+09:00">November 30, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1246. In my interview with the Foreign Minister today, he prefaced our
                    conversation by expressing his apologies for his unavailable [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">unavoidable?</hi>] delay in replying to previous
                    representations respecting Japanese interference with American rights and
                    interests in China. He said that he had started a full investigation of these
                    cases but had been ill with threatened pneumonia for some time. He, however,
                    expected to make a full report to me during the coming week.<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d593-f1"/> I replied that I would be interested in receiving his
                    report but that concrete results would carry more weight than explanations or
                    assurances for the future.</p>
                <pb facs="0563" n="555" xml:id="pg555"/>
                <p>Sent to the Department via Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Chungking and
                    Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d593-f1" n="44" xml:id="d593-f1-content">
                <p>For the Ambassador’s memorandum of his conversation with the Japanese Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs, December 17, see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_895"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 895</ref>; for oral statements by the
                    Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, December 17, see <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_895"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., pp.
                        895</ref> and <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_899">899</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
